    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented rejection of owners whose email domain is on a disposable-domain blocklist, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsurePostcodeValidForCity` validator).\n\n**New files:**\n- `rest/function/owner/EnsureEmailDomainAllowed.java` \u2014 validation step. Reads the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` via `@Val`, extracts the domain after the last `@`, and throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` if it matches the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Skips when email is absent (email is optional) or malformed (shape is left to `@Email`).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 checked exception (extends `Exception` so it appears in the `throws` clause).\n- `rest/escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` (mirrors `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`).\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted the `ensureEmailDomainAllowed` step right after `validate` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` (carrying `govern: [ transaction ]` on the PUT step to match its neighbours).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
