    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a near-exact structural clone of the codebase's established validation-step idiom, and that's the right call here.\n\n- **Logic is in the right unit.** `EnsureEmailDomainAllowed` is a single-purpose function class matching the existing `Ensure*` family (`EnsurePostcodeValidForCity`, `EnsureCityCapacity`, `EnsureDailyRegistrationLimit`), with one public `service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto)` method \u2014 exactly the OfficeFloor step shape AGENTS.md prescribes and the same `service` method name its siblings use.\n- **The exception/handler/escalation trio mirrors the existing `InvalidPostcode*` set precisely**: a checked exception carrying `rejectedValue` + a context field, a handler that reuses the shared `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper and sets `field`/`rejectedValue` properties, and a `officefloor/escalation/<FQN>.yml`. Nothing is reinvented; the shared `ProblemDetails` helper is reused rather than duplicated.\n- **No catch-all growth.** The new logic went into a new dedicated class rather than being bolted onto `ValidateOwner` or an existing step; the blocklist is a small local `Set.of(...)` constant, which is proportionate (there's no pre-existing shared source to reuse, unlike `CityRegions`).\n- **Wiring is consistent.** The step is inserted after `validate` in both `owners.POST.yml` and `{ownerId}.PUT.yml`, and the `govern: [ transaction ]` marker is applied on the PUT step to match the surrounding governed pipeline (and correctly omitted on POST, matching its neighbors).\n- **The \"validate only when present\" convention** and doc-comment style match `EnsurePostcodeValidForCity` verbatim, so a maintainer would find it immediately familiar.",
